    "created_at": "2022-07-27T05:17:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-27T05:17:53Z",
    "body": "I agree the preparation-time document check will never fail for import maps. This is a general programming pattern where you put shared logic inside a shared function (in this case \"execute the script element\"), even if for some inputs to that function, the logic is not necessary.\r\n\r\nI don't think it's a good idea to restructure the specification so that execution of the import map happens during the preparation phase, instead of the execution phase. Even if the results are observably the same, it makes the specification much harder to read and follow.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1196276156/reactions",
